DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/book-talk-prof-cecile-alduy-i
 n-conversation-with-prof-josh-landy\n\nThe French and Italian Department a
 nd French Speaking Worlds: Here and Now present: A Book talk on D’abord 
 ils sont venus chercher les mots [First They Came for Words]\, les Arènes
 \, 2026\, by Prof. Cécile Alduy\, in conversation with Prof. Joshua Landy
 . \n\nAn Author Caught Up by Her Subject\nA professor of literature at Sta
 nford and a discourse analysis scholar\, Cécile Alduy has spent years ana
 lyzing how the far right wages its culture war. In 2022\, in La Langue de 
 Zemmour (Zemmour’s Language)\, she showed how the presidential candidate
  was distorting concepts and history to short-circuit rational thinking an
 d appeal to hatred and fear. Then\, on January 20\, 2025\, her research ca
 ught up with her brutally. At Stanford\, her life and work were upended\, 
 like those of colleagues\, students and workers in universities\, schools\
 , administrations\, and scientific labs nationwide\, when the new administ
 ration unleashed terror and censorship on culture and science. In this fir
 st-person account\, she tells what the far right does once in power\, day 
 to day.\n\nA New Linguistic and Political Regime\n“Women\,” “climate
  crisis\,” “disability\,” “diversity\,” “Black\,” “equalit
 y\,” “gender\,” “social justice\,” “LGBT\,” “prejudice\,
 ” “racism\,” “vaccine” ... These words\, among others\, have bee
 n banned or blacklisted by the Trump administration since March 2025. Céc
 ile Alduy conducts a gripping investigation into this list\, which grew fr
 om a handful of demonized terms into over 480 flammable ones through antic
 ipatory 
